WEBVTT

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.360
You boys really are the worst, aren't you'?

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.780
You talk about marriage, then just 
grab all the money you can...

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.000
How about you tell me what else 
you did? In your own words!

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.650
W-We had him attack her...

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.810
And then?

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.130
We recorded it... distributed it....

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.650
You wanna tell me what that feels like?

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.510
To betray someone who trusted you?

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.650
Welcome home, Lin-chan.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.430
Not gonna say "I'm home"?

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.780
Weren't you taught how important 
that stuff is at school?

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.240
Nope.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.830
I mean, you come home 
after being out all night,

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:59.700
and in a short skirt like that, no less...

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.720
Shut the hell up. What are you, my mom?

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.870
Talking like some pampered princess
who thinks the world is here for her...

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.670
I had work, remember?

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.170
Oh, helping Jiro out?

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.260
You ended up accepting, then.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.840
The summer heat is kicking Maru in the ass.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.830
Guess that makes you a pinch hitter.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.220
Yeah.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.780
The guy was a real shithead.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.690
<i>He hit another two home runs today, putting 
him right out in front in the home run derby.</i>

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.780
<i>He's matched his own record from last year.</i>

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.140
Forty homers! Ain't that something?

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.910
I'd better catch up!

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.310
I'm off to the batting cage.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.660
Why are you competing with pros?

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.630
I'm off!

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.300
On your way back, could 
you get toilet paper...

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:02.070
Are we out? Pretty considerate 
of you to bring that up, Lin-chan.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:03.930
Oh, shut up.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.090
Where's my "Have a safe trip"?

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.370
Just get out of here!

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.070
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.030
I'm getting considerate, huh?

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.350
Guess I'm getting immersed 
in the pampered life, too.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.520
<b>#09  Hit and Run</b>

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.330
Ever the slow starter, huh?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:14.980
Shut up. And if you've brought me 
another cheap job, you're in for it.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.570
Am I now?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.850
This is all because you got on the 
Kakyu Association's bad side, you know.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.710
That's the reason our clients 
want to stay at arm's length.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.930
Not my fault.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.230
They're looking a little blunt...

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.330
Need some maintenance. You realize 
these are the tools of your trade, right?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.640
They're all disposable, though.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.040
Even if they are, they need to be in 
good shape when you use them.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.250
You've always been rough with your tools...

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:48.300
Even though I'm always telling you,
"Take better care of your tools."

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.100
What are you actually here for?

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.980
There's someone I'm in contact with...

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.350
Someone from an organization in Hong Kong.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:02.030
They seem to know about our 
bad blood with the Kakyu Association,

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.480
which could make this rather interesting.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.490
You think?

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:11.540
You never change. Have a little faith in me.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.150
Come here. Don't be scared.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.980
What? You still haven't 
taught him our signs?

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.720
I thought you were gonna teach him.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.620
When you say "signs," you mean...

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.650
Like this?

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.790
Yep, that's it. For instance...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.940
That's the sign telling 
you to steal a base.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.900
How am I supposed to remember that?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.390
Once you know the key, the rest is simple.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.110
For us, it's the belt.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:53.020
And wherever you touch 
after that is the real sign.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.920
The rest are all fakes.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.170
If the ear is touched after the belt, 
that's the sign for stealing a base.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.120
The hat tells you to bunt.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:00.830
You get it?

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.290
Sorta...

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.050
Really?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.190
What was that?

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.190
Bunt.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.620
Bingo!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.020
Also, if the chest is the next thing touched 
after the belt, that's the sign for a hit and run.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.610
"Hit and run"?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.900
Probably faster to just demonstrate.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.110
Shit!

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.330
Hey, come on! You can't turn back!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.290
Huh? But he missed!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.760
Doesn't matter. When you get 
the sign, you've gotta run.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.970
If you worry about the batter, 
you'll get a late start.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.780
What if it leads to an out?

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.960
If it happens, it happens.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.720
That's baseball for you.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.680
Baseball's a real pain in the ass.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.740
When you get the sign for a hit and run,

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:03.350
you have to run, and put your 
faith in your teammates.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.520
Trust that they'll be able to handle it.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.570
Faith in your teammates, huh?

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.620
The only person you can trust is yourself.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:22.550
Lin, if you're feeling out of it, 
go take a breather.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.540
Y-Yeah...

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.220
<i>Qiaomei?</i>

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.810
You're going to be in real trouble soon.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.270
I mean, you have two kids, don't you?

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.860
Keep coming if you want, 
but my answer won't change!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.110
I'm not letting go of either—

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.990
But if you sold just one of them, 
you'd have a much easier life!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.480
You could even go see a doctor.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.960
Go! Get out of here!

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:04.780
Big brother?

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.170
It's okay, Qiaomei.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.940
There's nothing to be scared of.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.050
Big brother!

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.020
Big brother Maomei!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:25.150
<i>Qiaomei... Mom...</i>

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.510
If you're cold, you can huddle up closer.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.710
It's not that. I'm scared.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.490
What's gonna happen to us?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:49.780
I've heard that we're actually 
better off being sold to rich people.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.950
Anyone else might chop us 
up and sell our organs.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:57.450
That's not true! I heard that 
we're going to school.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:00.470
A school for killers.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:01.510
Killers?

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.640
That's a lie!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.280
It's true.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:09.230
They're gonna train us up and 
turn us into assassins and soldiers.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.540
And even that's better 
than what some kids get.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.800
Looks like a prison, doesn't it?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:42.810
Apparently, it was one once, 
but now it's just a factory...

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:48.310
A factory to turn you boys into killers.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:01.830
Get out.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:06.080
One of the trainees died, 
so you get to fill his spot.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.080
Go in there and work hard.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:14.570
Hey!

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.420
Come here.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.730
Listen well.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.940
My word is law here.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:33.660
Understood?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.570
For the next five years, you're going 
to be trained in how to survive.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.030
Never trust anyone else.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.500
The only person you can trust is yourself.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.460
That's the best lesson you'll learn here....

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:51.920
Hell, it'll probably be the best lesson 
you learn in your whole life.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.980
Remember it.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.530
Get in.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.050
I said get in!

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.170
Hey, newbie.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.340
I'm Feilang. Nice to meet you.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:39.800
I'm Maomei. Likewise.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.900
The pleasure's all mine, Mao.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.060
Does that hurt?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.020
No...

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:53.570
If it does, you can cry all you want.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:56.690
Not that I'll be able to do anything for ya.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:03.010
Around here, everything's 
done in teams of two.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:08.160
It's all about mutual responsibility, so you 
gotta get used to helping each other out.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.030
Teams of two...

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:12.590
Yeah, for training and studying.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:18.710
I had a partner before, 
but he committed suicide.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.710
I woke up and saw him hanging over there.

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:28.140
Probably couldn't deal with the training.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:31.870
Which is why we should help each other out.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.850
It's only five years, right, partner?

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:43.860
One!

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:44.450
Two!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.020
Three!

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:45.700
Four!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.220
Five!

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:46.810
Six!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:47.450
Seven!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.370
Eight.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.670
Run! Who said you could stop?!

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.060
What the hell?

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.660
It's fine. That's just how it works here.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:09.680
But...

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:13.990
No resting!

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.980
What's with that look? Feeling defiant?

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.940
We're sorry, sir!

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.250
Here, get on. I'll carry you.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:27.810
But I—

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:28.730
Hurry up!

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:36.390
So long as we're here, 
we're two halves of a whole.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.600
I'm amazed you have the energy to whistle...

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.100
You'll get used to it.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.770
Listen, Feilang, about today... Thanks.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.430
Don't sweat it.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.440
How'd you end up here, anyway?

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:12.140
How? We were poor... and in debt...

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:13.620
They sold you?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:14.450
No!

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.380
I sold myself.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.140
I lied to my mom about getting a job.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.420
Why do that?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:30.100
No matter how poor we were, 
Mom refused to sell me or my sister.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:32.690
She always tried to protect us.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.750
I thought that was enough...

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.310
That no matter what else 
happened, it would be enough.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.770
I see...

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.010
What about you?

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.950
I was sold by my parents.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:56.270
My mom was a hooker, and they tried 
to use me to bring in business...

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:02.490
But there's not much a boy 
can do to help with that.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:08.820
But I'm glad I came here.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.730
Compared to how my life used to be,
this is a huge improvement.

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:16.180
That's why I'm going to survive this.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:18.710
No matter what it takes.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.800
Don't endure the pain! Endure the fear!

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.550
If you let the pain in, you'll start talking!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.720
Do not fear! Resist!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:40.770
<b>4 Years Later</b>

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:44.770
Did you see the rankings?

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.380
Yeah. Our team was at the top.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.320
Say, Mao...

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.750
Something's been on my mind.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:57.670
Wanna work together 
once we get out of here?

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.050
It might not be possible right away,

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:04.260
but one day, we can work 
together, make a ton of money,

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:07.000
and enjoy every day of our lives.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.630
I like the sound of that.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:11.920
No one can stop us if we work together.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:16.680
When that happens, you 
should come by my house.

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:19.640
I want to introduce you to my family.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:23.100
Something wrong?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.640
No, I'll come. Can't wait.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.950
Thanks, Feilang.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.360
I only made it this far because of you.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:37.990
Let's work hard on that final 
exam and pass it together.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:44.250
Yeah. Let's pass it and get out of here.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:45.710
Together.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.310
The two of us!

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.560
This is your final exam.

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.050
There's no time limit.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.420
The one who kills his opponent wins.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.890
Kills?

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:00.390
You're joking, right?!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.050
No holds barred.

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:04.600
You may use any weapons you find.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.450
Begin.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:07.560
Screw this!

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.720
This isn't funny!

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.900
Would you rather both be disqualified?

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.390
Let us out, damn it!

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.290
Mao! You—

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.670
Fight, Feilang!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.550
I'm gonna smash the lock with an ax!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.110
You go get a weapon, too!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.310
One more ought to...

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.170
Feilang... Why?

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.030
You're asking me why?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.910
Isn't this how the exam works?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:14.940
Do you remember what I told you 
when you first came here?

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.780
About the guy before you killing himself?

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.680
That was a lie.

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:25.210
I killed him.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:33.700
I happened to hear what 
the final exam would be.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:44.530
I thought making it look like 
suicide would get me out of it.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:47.540
But then you showed up.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.490
Sucks to be me.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:57.920
I trusted you... We helped each other...

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:02.380
Did you forget? The only person 
you can trust is yourself.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:06.260
You'd make a lousy hitman, pal.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:10.340
So long, Mao.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:39.940
Gonna... get out of here...

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.330
No one... can stop me...

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:55.560
Congratulations. You've all passed the exam.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.790
You've cast aside your humanity 
and become full-fledged weapons.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:01.810
Congratulations.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:07.490
Lin!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.860
Where's my "thank you"?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.750
I backed you up! Show some gratitude.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.460
Pampered as hell...

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.290
That sure was fast.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:26.420
An employment exam.

00:22:25.480 --> 00:22:27.130
A famous leader in the Kakyu Association.

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:28.530
The Submarine Ninja?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:30.200
Now that is fine!

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:30.880
A katana?

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:31.700
It's over.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:34.080
Feels like something good 
is gonna happen today.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:00.520
<b>Beijing, China</b>

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:08.890
I'll be taking the virus.

00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:13.830
Along with this.

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:21.040
Do you know where he is?

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:23.930
Japan? Hakata?

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.100
Got it. Send me the details.

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:31.170
Won't be long now...

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:34.620
I'll see you again soon, Mao.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:41.060
#10  Shortstop
